## Tutorials

Usenew ArrayBuffer()to create a new ArrayBuffer.

The ArrayBuffer does not have methods toreadandwritedata.

You must always use aviewto access the data.

Typed ArraysandDataViewsprovide a way to read and write numeric values to an
ArrayBuffer.

Common typed arrays are:

ADataViewis a more flexible view for an ArrayBuffer.

ADataViewlets you read and write values of different types (Int8, Uint16, Float32, etc.).

ADataViewalso lets you read and write values at any byte offset.

You can make a copy of a part of anArrayBufferusing
theslice()method. It returns a newArrayBufferwith bytes from the specified range.

AnArrayBufferis not shared between threads by default.

To share memory between workers, JavaScript providesSharedArrayBuffer.

It behaves likeArrayBuffer, but its contents can be shared and
used withAtomics.

### Code Examples

